#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:2
msgid "Inheritance"
msgstr "Nasljeđivanje"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:4
msgid ""
"Inheritance lets a class *extend* another class -- start with all of its "
"methods and attributes, then add or override what is different. The original"
" is called the *base* (or *parent*); the extension is called the *subclass*."
msgstr ""
"Nasljeđivanje omogućuje klasi da *proširi* drugu klasu -- da počne sa svim "
"njezinim metodama i atributima, a zatim doda ili nadjača ono što je "
"drukčije. Original se naziva *baza* (ili *roditelj*\\ ); proširenje se "
"naziva *podklasa*\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:9
msgid ""
"A base class Shape pointing down to a subclass Square;\n"
"Square overrides one method (area) and inherits the\n"
"rest."
msgstr ""
"Bazna klasa Shape pokazuje prema dolje na podklasu Square;\n"
"Square nadjačava jednu metodu (area) i nasljeđuje\n"
"ostalo."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:14
msgid ""
"``Square`` reuses every method on ``Shape`` and overrides the ones it needs "
"to specialise."
msgstr ""
"``Square`` ponovno koristi svaku metodu na ``Shape`` i nadjačava one koje "
"treba specijalizirati."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:18
msgid "Defining a subclass"
msgstr "Definiranje podklase"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:20
msgid "The base class goes in the parentheses on the ``class`` line:"
msgstr "Bazna klasa ide u zagrade na retku ``class``\\ :"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:45
msgid "Output::"
msgstr "Izlaz::"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:49
msgid ""
"``Square`` inherits ``describe`` from ``Shape`` unchanged and overrides "
"``area`` to return a real value. The base's ``describe`` still works because"
" it calls ``self.area()`` -- which resolves to the override at run time."
msgstr ""
"``Square`` nepromijenjeno nasljeđuje ``describe`` od ``Shape`` i nadjačava "
"``area`` da vrati stvarnu vrijednost. Bazna metoda ``describe`` i dalje radi"
" jer poziva ``self.area()`` -- što se u vrijeme izvođenja razrješava na "
"nadjačanu metodu."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:55
msgid "super()"
msgstr "super()"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:57
msgid ""
":func:`super` returns a proxy that lets a method call the base-class version"
" of a method. The most common use is calling the base ``__init__`` from a "
"subclass ``__init__`` so the base gets to initialise its own attributes:"
msgstr ""
":func:`super` vraća proxy koji omogućuje metodi da pozove baznu verziju "
"metode. Najčešća upotreba je pozivanje baznog ``__init__`` iz ``__init__`` "
"podklase kako bi baza inicijalizirala vlastite atribute:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:69
msgid ""
"Forgetting ``super().__init__`` is a common source of bugs: attributes the "
"base would have set never get set, and the inherited methods that rely on "
"them crash later."
msgstr ""
"Zaboravljanje ``super().__init__`` čest je izvor grešaka: atributi koje bi "
"baza postavila nikad se ne postave, a naslijeđene metode koje se na njih "
"oslanjaju kasnije se sruše."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:74
msgid "The implicit base class"
msgstr "Implicitna bazna klasa"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:76
msgid ""
"Every class implicitly inherits from :class:`object`, the root of Python's "
"type hierarchy. Methods like :meth:`__repr__ <object.__repr__>`, "
":meth:`__eq__ <object.__eq__>`, and the machinery behind attribute access "
"all come from there even when a class declares no base. Writing ``class "
"Foo(object):`` explicitly and writing ``class Foo:`` are equivalent in "
"modern Python; the latter is the conventional form."
msgstr ""
"Svaka klasa implicitno nasljeđuje od :class:`object`\\ , korijena Pythonove "
"hijerarhije tipova. Metode poput :meth:`__repr__ <object.__repr__>`\\ , "
":meth:`__eq__ <object.__eq__>` i mehanizam iza pristupa atributima sve "
"potječu odande čak i kad klasa ne deklarira nijednu bazu. Eksplicitno "
"pisanje ``class Foo(object):`` i pisanje ``class Foo:`` ekvivalentni su u "
"modernom Pythonu; potonji je konvencionalni oblik."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:85
msgid "When inheritance helps -- and when it does not"
msgstr "Kada nasljeđivanje pomaže -- a kada ne"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:87
msgid ""
"Use inheritance when one class is genuinely a *more specific kind* of "
"another, sharing most of the behaviour. The classic test is the \"is-a\" "
"check: a ``Square`` is a ``Shape``."
msgstr ""
"Koristi nasljeđivanje kad je jedna klasa stvarno *specifičnija vrsta* druge,"
" dijeleći većinu ponašanja. Klasični test je provjera \"jest-a\": ``Square``"
" jest ``Shape``\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:91
msgid ""
"When two classes just happen to share a few helpers, inheritance is "
"overkill. Reach for *composition* instead: have one class hold an instance "
"of the other as an attribute and use it through that attribute. The shape is"
" \"has-a\", not \"is-a\":"
msgstr ""
"Kad se dvije klase tek slučajno dijele nekoliko pomoćnika, nasljeđivanje je "
"pretjerano. Posegni umjesto toga za *kompozicijom*\\ : neka jedna klasa drži"
" instancu druge kao atribut i koristi je kroz taj atribut. Oblik je "
"\"ima-a\", ne \"jest-a\":"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:115
msgid "Both work. The composing version is usually better because it:"
msgstr "Oba rade. Verzija s kompozicijom obično je bolja jer:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:117
msgid ""
"**Keeps interfaces small.** ``WorkerComposes`` exposes only ``run`` and "
"``logger``. ``WorkerInherits`` also exposes ``log`` -- callers can write "
"``worker.log(...)`` directly, whether or not that was intended."
msgstr ""
"**Drži sučelja malenima.** ``WorkerComposes`` izlaže samo ``run`` i "
"``logger``\\ . ``WorkerInherits`` izlaže i ``log`` -- pozivatelji mogu "
"izravno pisati ``worker.log(...)``\\ , bilo da je to bilo namjeravano ili "
"ne."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:121
msgid ""
"**Decouples lifetimes.** The logger can be swapped, shared between workers, "
"or constructed differently per worker, all without touching the ``Worker`` "
"class. A subclass is bolted to its base."
msgstr ""
"**Razdvaja životne vijekove.** Logger se može zamijeniti, dijeliti među "
"radnicima ili konstruirati drukčije po radniku, sve to bez diranja klase "
"``Worker``\\ . Podklasa je pričvršćena za svoju bazu."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:125
msgid ""
"**Avoids method-name collisions.** Two bases that both define ``run`` clash "
"when a class tries to inherit from both; two attributes never clash."
msgstr ""
"**Izbjegava sudare imena metoda.** Dvije baze koje obje definiraju ``run`` "
"sudaraju se kad klasa pokuša naslijediti od obje; dva atributa nikad se ne "
"sudaraju."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:129
msgid "A practical rule of thumb:"
msgstr "Praktično pravilo:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:131
msgid ""
"Use inheritance when the subclass really *is* a kind of the base and every "
"method on the base makes sense on it too -- ``Square`` is a ``Shape``; "
"``MemoryError`` is an ``Exception``."
msgstr ""
"Koristi nasljeđivanje kad podklasa stvarno *jest* vrsta baze i kad svaka "
"metoda na bazi ima smisla i na njoj -- ``Square`` jest ``Shape``\\ ; "
"``MemoryError`` jest ``Exception``\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/classes/inheritance.rst:135
msgid ""
"Use composition for everything else -- when you just want the *behaviour* of"
" another class, not its identity. Most real code uses composition far more "
"than it uses inheritance."
msgstr ""
"Koristi kompoziciju za sve ostalo -- kad želiš samo *ponašanje* druge klase,"
" a ne njezin identitet. Većina stvarnog koda koristi kompoziciju daleko više"
" nego nasljeđivanje."
